  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Peace and Justice (PPJ)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  The Promoting Peace and Justice (PPJ) activity improves delivery of legal aid, strengthens the capacity of the lower judiciary, promotes excellence in justice delivery, and increases citizen awareness of the rights available through formal justice institutions.  To advance the Government of Bangladesh&apos;s priority of expanding access to justice, USAID will continue to provide technical assistance and training to legal-aid committees that operate under the Supreme Court, labor courts, and district courts. The activity will also continue to develop awareness campaigns and disseminate information to citizens about the availability of legal aid and mediation services.  PPJ will also support policy reforms by conducting culturally appropriate judicial training programs to introduce and implement the International Framework for Court Excellence, a tool for assessing the performance of courts.  This IM contributes to Freedom of Expressions ($500K) and DRG ($1.5M) earmarks..This activity will be in line with the State-USAID Integrated Country Strategy (ICS) Mission Goal Two and the U.S. government development objective of improved democratic systems that promote transparency, accountability, and integrity..</narrative>
  </description>
